# A plugin is installed by a git checkout on the user's machine, and its scripts run where they land.
# Git for Windows checks files out with CRLF line endings unless told otherwise (core.autocrlf=true is
# its installer's default), and a shell script with them fails in Git Bash (#440): the scripts in a
# plugin's bin folder stay LF. A .cmd file is the other way round: cmd.exe wants CRLF.
plugins/*/bin/** text eol=lf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
